  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Satan Speeds Up**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **kglw2023-06-11** (recommended): soundboard; 15 songs; 117 min [1]\n- **kglw2023-06-11.vwmule**: source not stated; 15 songs; 118 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Challenging wind conditions caused fluctuations in the recording quality despite the performance [4]\n- **kglw2023-06-11.dankski**: source not stated; 15 songs; 118 min; rated 3/5 by 1 [3]. Said about its sound: Wind gusts caused the recording's volume and tone to fluctuate significantly [5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Audience member Seb was brought onstage to perform the vocal intro [1]\n- The song was dedicated to John Mayer, referred to as the guitar slayer [1]\n- Included quotes from Got My Mojo Working, Sweet Home Chicago, and My Babe [1]\n- The outdoor venue experienced a chilly and very windy night with strong phasing [2]\n- This was the first of three sold-out nights at the Salt Shed [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **kglw2023-06-11**: taped by Sam Joseph, Nico Wilson, Gaspard Demulemeester and Joseph Santarpia; transferred by MaxEgg; source: SBD > WAV [1]\n- **kglw2023-06-11.vwmule**: taped by Alex Leary; transferred by Alex Leary; source: DPA 4023 > Sound Devices MixPre-6 (24/48) [2]\n- **kglw2023-06-11.dankski**: taped by DankskiVision; transferred by DankskiVision; source: Zoom H6 Shotgun 24/48 [3]",
